      "text_raw": "To illustrate this last point,\nlet us take this well known\nsymmetrical opamp.\nFor a capacitive load, it\nis obvious that the output\ncan reach rail-to-rail output\nvoltages. At the extremities,\nthe output transistor goes\ninto the linear region and\nthe gain is reduced leading\nto distortion. It is still rail-\nto-rail, however.\nAt the input, it is clear\nthat a voltage is lost of\nV +V for the input\nGS1 DSsat9\nrange, which is rather large.\nSome other circuitry is now required.\nIs this always required?",
